{"id":"assistant-4dc33244-0354-571a-84f9-33595e28bfb6","sessionId":"fca6269e-2e27-c7b8-cefa-fba47dfc3393","turnId":"turn-f5909b6cd1837087f8f62dedb727a527","inputEntryId":"user-turn-f5909b6cd1837087f8f62dedb727a527-1","createdAt":1794285417073,"updatedAt":1794285417073,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Everything is in place. Let me create a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. Here's what was changed:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Modified `/private/tmp/h-PGXPOT/bot.py`**: Updated the `build_system` function to return **two separate cache blocks** instead of one concatenated block:\n   - Block 1: Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (byte-stable, never changes)\n   - Block 2: Dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` (volatile, changes with memory writes)\n\n2. **Created `/private/tmp/h-PGXPOT/ANSWER.md`**: Documented the fix and explained which parts of the colleague's note applied.\n\n### How it works:\n\nPreviously, when `save_fact` was called, it modified the athlete's facts, which changed the entire system prompt block. Since Anthropic's prompt cache uses prefix hashing, any byte change invalidates everything from that point to the end of the cached block. This meant the entire system prompt (including the static instructions) was evicted from cache on every memory write.\n\nWith the fix, the system prompt is split into two cache blocks. When `save_fact` modifies the facts, only the second block (the volatile athlete context) is invalidated. The first block (static instructions) remains cached, reducing the cache miss penalty from ~1000 tokens to ~240 tokens (the size of the volatile tail).\n\n### What applied from the colleague's note:\n\n- Two cache_control segments\n- Prefix hash behavior understanding\n- Static block must be byte-stable\n- Volatile tail ordering (already satisfied)\n- Resist per-message personalization (already applied)\n\n### What didn't apply:\n\n- Tool filtering (already implemented)\n- Anthropic SDK specifics (provider-agnostic fix)\n- Usage verification steps (structural change only)"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
